}
{\plain {\b Exercise 31.1}{  Show that the
 resulting maximum of (31.5), using (31.6),
 is real and    that it is in fact the }{\b 
energy}{, the integral of the squared modulus,
 of the pulse            complex modulation
 f(t). Show that the energy of the complex
 pulse modulation is twice the energy of
 the real pulse modulation.}}
}
.TXT 11 0 351 0
Cg a62.250000,62.375000,330
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
{\f1\fnil Symbol;}
}
{\plain {\b Exercise 31.2}{  The filter 
IR of (31.6) is complex. Show how this filtering
