{\plain {If an object is moving with a component
 v of its velocity }{\b v}{ along its line
 of sight to the radar then there will be
 a }{\b Doppler shift}{ }{\f1 n}{ in the
 frequency of the received pulse given by
 }{\f1 n}{ = (2v/c)}{\f1 n}{\fs16 \dn6 c}{.
 Thus, the radar can estimate this velocity
 by measuring the Doppler shift. The }{\b 
range-Doppler-finding radar signal model}{
 is now}}
}
